PS+=['Mr. Green teaches at a junior high school. He shared some important facts about World Water Day and clean water in his class on March 22.\nMr. Green: Good morning, students. Today is World Water Day. The first World Water Day was in 1993. This holiday is a day to celebrate water and to think about water problems around the world.\nMr. Green: Now work in groups of six and talk about this question: Why is water important?\nMr. Green: Good! Let’s see. Hmm, you have good points, students.\n(Picture on the screen: Water is important — for drinking / for cleaning / for growing plants / for cooking / for making energy / for staying healthy)\nMr. Green: We all need water. We’re lucky to have clean water when we want it. However, about 785 million people in the world do not have clean water to drink. Life is 【arduous】 for them. They often get sick because of drinking dirty water, and many of them even die. In some countries, many children have to walk hours every day to get water for their family. Because of this, they can’t go to school like all of you.\nMr. Green: So, World Water Day is also a day to think about poor people in other countries. What can we do to help more people to get clean water? Let’s talk about it in our next class.\n（energy 能源）']
