PS+=['Kevin, a junior high school student, loves potatoes. He is planning to visit Idaho Potato Museum during summer vacation. Last night, he found some interesting facts about potatoes and the museum on the Internet. The following are his notes.\n【potatoes】\n1. There are more than 4,000 kinds in the world.\n2. They come in different shapes and sizes.\n3. A potato is about 80% water and 20% solids.\n4. It is better to store them in a dry, dark place.\n5. They are a kind of vegetable and are good for health.\n6. Wash them only before cooking them.\n【Idaho Potato Museum】\n• opened in 1988\n• shows the history of potatoes in Idaho and many interesting things about this plant\n• has a gift shop and a coffee shop\n【Where】130 NW Main Street, Blackfoot, ID 83221, USA\n【Opening hours】\nSeptember～May: 9:30a.m.～5:00p.m. Mon-Sat\nJune～August: 9:30a.m.～7:00p.m. Mon-Sat; 9:30a.m.～5:00p.m. Sun\nClosed: Thanksgiving, Christmas & New Year’s Day\n【Tickets】\nAdults: $6　Seniors: $5.50　Children 5-12: $3　Children 4 & Under: Free　Groups of 15 or more: $5 each\n（potato 馬鈴薯　solid 固體　store 儲存　adult 成人　senior 老年人）']
