PS+=['Jason is interested in electric cars. Last week he made a report about these modern cars.\n【What are electric cars?】\nElectric cars do not run on gas. They use battery power to heat and cool. It usually takes 300 smartphone batteries to make one battery for an electric car.\n【Who made the first electric car in the world?】\nAround 1832-1839, Robert Anderson built an early electric car.\n【How were the sales of electric cars in the world from 2019 to 2022?】\nSee picture 1.（長條圖：2019 年約 7,000,000 輛出頭，2020 年約 10,000,000 輛，2021 年約 16,000,000 輛，2022 年約 26,000,000 輛）\n【Top 5 countries with the most electric cars for every 1,000 residents in 2020】\nIn 2020, electric cars already became more common around the world, especially in countries like Sweden, Iceland, Norway, Germany, and the Netherlands. Of the five countries, Norway was far ahead, with the most electric cars for every 1,000 residents. Iceland and Sweden were next. Electric cars were more popular in Iceland than in Sweden. Germany and the Netherlands had the fewest electric cars. There were 10.7 electric cars for every 1,000 residents in the Netherlands and 8.5 in Germany.\n【What are the good points and bad points of electric cars?】\nGood points: *They are cleaner and quieter than gas-powered cars. *They save money on gas. *Some electric cars can really go very fast.\nBad points: *They can be very expensive. *Charging electric cars is slow. It may take at least 30 minutes to get 80% charged. *The battery may become weak over time.\n（electric 電的　battery 電池　resident 居民　especially 特別地　charge 充電）']
