PS+=['Isabella Wilson is from the US. She has a great job, and she likes it very much.\nSeveral years ago, Isabella got her first job, and then she began to work 80-100 hours a week. One day, she thought to herself, “What a life! I work, work, and work! I’m really sick of all this. I want more sunshine, more exercise, and more time to myself.” Then and there, she decided to leave her job.\nIsabella loved traveling, and she dreamed of visiting many parts of the world. In 2017, after she quit her job, she traveled across the US, but she had to think of ways to cut down on expenses. Then in July, 2018, in a book, she found out an interesting job, house sitting.\nAt the end of 2018, she began to work as a house sitter. What does she do? She stays at and looks after a house when its owners are away. At the same time, she has to take care of their pets. In this way, she stays in an expensive house for free. She can cook, take a bath, and even use the owner’s car to go around. Best of all, she can make some money from the job.\n“It’s cost-saving,” Isabella said. For example, in 2020, she took her first trip to the UK for a month without having to spend at least £200 a night at a hotel.\nNow, Isabella enjoys her life very much. She is planning to write a book about her experience as a house sitter.\n（travel 旅行　quit 離開；辭職　expense 開銷）']
