PS+=['Climbing Mount Everest, the highest mountain in the world, is a big dream for many climbers. In 1953, Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay became the first people to get to the top of the mountain. From then on, ＿41＿. Now, over 600 people attempt it every climbing season during a few weeks of the year when the weather is just right.\nBecause Mount Everest stands at 8,849 m, the air there is very thin and cold. ＿42＿. In fact, not every climber can make it. Sadly, some of them might even lose their lives in their attempt. Every year about 5-10 people die on Mount Everest, and the number is rising each year.\nWhen climbers climb Mount Everest, they must carry a lot of things with them. Bottles of oxygen are one of the most important things to keep them safe. They also have to take tents, food, and many other things. Sadly, many of the climbers do not clean up themselves when going down the mountain, and they leave behind what they no longer need behind them. In a lot of pictures, we can see that ＿43＿.\nFrom now on, for the good of nature every climber to Mount Everest should stop leaving trash there. This way, they can enjoy the trip and help the mountain stay clean at the same time.\n（attempt 試圖　oxygen 氧氣　tent 帳篷）']
